      <title>Global wind farms are associated with land use dependent asymmetric warming and ecological changes</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s43247-026-04195-3</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Communications Earth &amp;amp; Environment, Published online: 13 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s43247-026-04195-3"&gt;doi:10.1038/s43247-026-04195-3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Wind farms increase nighttime temperatures and reduce vegetation productivity in a land-use-dependent manner, according to explainable machine learning and structural equation modeling of decades of observations from tens of thousands of wind farms worldwide.</content:encoded>
